.TH OTPME-DICTIONARY 1 "2025-12-29" "OTPme 0.3.0a120" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme-dictionary \- manage OTPme dictionaries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme-dictionary
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIdictionary\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otpme-dictionary
manages dictionaries in the OTPme system. Dictionaries are word lists used by password policies for password strength checking and passphrase generation. Supported dictionary types are
.BR list ,
.BR sorted-list ,
and
.BR guessing .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Dictionary Management
.TP
.B add \fIdictionary\fR \fR[\fIdict_type\fR]
Create a new dictionary, optionally with a specific type.
.TP
.B del \fIdictionary\fR
Delete a dictionary.
.TP
.B show \fR[\fIdictionary\fR]
Display dictionary information. Without arguments, shows all dictionaries.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIregex\fR]
List dictionaries, optionally filtered by regex pattern.
.TP
.B enable \fIdictionary\fR
Enable a disabled dictionary.
.TP
.B disable \fIdictionary\fR
Disable a dictionary without deleting it.
.TP
.B rename \fIdictionary\fR \fInew_name\fR
Rename a dictionary.
.TP
.B move \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-acls\fR] \fIdictionary\fR \fIunit\fR
Move dictionary to a different unit.
.TP
.B touch \fIdictionary\fR
Re-index the object to fix potential index problems.
.SS Word Management
.TP
.B word_import \fIdictionary\fR \fIfile\fR
Import words from a file into the dictionary.
.TP
.B word_learning \fIdictionary\fR \fIfile\fR
Analyze words from a file and build a guessing dictionary with character sequence patterns and their frequencies.
.TP
.B word_export \fIdictionary\fR
Export all words to stdout.
.TP
.B clear \fIdictionary\fR
Remove all words from the dictionary.
.SS Object Changelog
Every change to the object writes an entry: who made it, when, and what was done.
A change can carry a comment of its own, through the global option \fB\-\-changelog\fR.
.PP
An \fIentry_id\fR is the number the listing shows in front of an entry, counted from 0.
.PP
Only the comment of an entry can be changed or removed.
What was done and by whom stays as it is.
.PP
A command that changes something asks first; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B changelog \fIdictionary\fR
Show the changelog of the dictionary.
Needs the ACL \fBview:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B edit_changelog \fIdictionary\fR \fIentry_id\fR \fIcomment\fR
Set the comment of that entry, or replace the one it has.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B del_changelog \fIdictionary\fR \fIentry_id\fR
Remove the comment of that entry.
The entry itself stays, and an entry without a comment is refused.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B clear_changelog \fIdictionary\fR
Remove every entry of the changelog.
.br
This needs more than the ACL \fBclear:changelog\fR: the config parameter
.B allow_changelog_clearing
has to allow it (see \fBotpme\fR(7)).
It is true by default, but where no value is found at all, clearing is refused.
OTPme asks the token you are signed in with first, then the object.
.SS Policy Management
A \fIpolicy\fR is the name of a policy, not a path.
It is looked for in the site of the dictionary.
Which policies there are, and what each of them does, is in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
.PP
Attaching and detaching ask before they change anything; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B add_policy \fIdictionary\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Attach a policy to the dictionary.
.br
A policy has a list of object types it is for; one that does not name \fBdictionary\fR is refused.
So is a second policy of a type that allows only one per object.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBassign:policy\fR.
.TP
.B remove_policy \fIdictionary\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Remove a policy from the dictionary.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBremove:policy\fR, and that one verbatim: a plain \fBremove\fR does not cover it.
Detaching a policy takes away what it enforces, so it must not be cheaper than attaching one.
.TP
.B list_policies \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIdictionary\fR
List the policies attached to the dictionary.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
Use \fB\-\-policy\-types\fR to list only policies of the given types; these are policy types, not policy names.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBview:policies\fR.
.SS ACL Management
.TP
.B add_acl \fIdictionary\fR \fIowner_type\fR \fIowner\fR \fIacl\fR
Add an access control entry.
.TP
.B del_acl \fIdictionary\fR \fIacl\fR
Remove an access control entry.
.TP
.B list_acls \fIdictionary\fR
Display all ACLs for the dictionary.
.TP
.B enable_acl_inheritance \fIdictionary\fR
Enable ACL inheritance from parent objects.
.TP
.B disable_acl_inheritance \fIdictionary\fR
Disable ACL inheritance.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B description \fIdictionary\fR \fR[\fIdescription\fR]
Set dictionary description.
.TP
.B info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIdictionary\fR \fR[\fIinfo\fR]
Set free-form info text. If \fIinfo\fR is omitted, the current info text is
opened in the editor specified by the \fBEDITOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B dump_info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIdictionary\fR
Dump the info text to stdout.
.SS Import/Export
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] \fIdictionary\fR
Export dictionary configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display Options
.TP
.B \-a
Show all dictionaries (across all units).
.TP
.B \-z \fISIZE\fR
Limit output size.
.TP
.B \-\-fields \fIFIELD1,FIELD2\fR
Display only specified fields.
.TP
.B \-\-policy\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of policies shown.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of items shown per object.
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-by \fIFIELD\fR
Sort output by field.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Output without headers/borders.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output as CSV.
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-sep \fISEP\fR
CSV separator character.
.TP
.B \-\-attribute \fIATTR\fR
Display specific attribute in list command.
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-acls
Preserve ACLs when moving dictionary.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Password for encrypting exports.
.PP
Global options are available for all commands. See
.BR otpme (1)
for details.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Managing Dictionaries
.TP
.B otpme-dictionary add english list
Create a word list dictionary
.TP
.B otpme-dictionary add english_guessing guessing
Create a guessing dictionary
.TP
.B otpme-dictionary word_import english /usr/share/dict/words
Import words from a file
.TP
.B otpme-dictionary word_learning english_guessing /usr/share/dict/words
Build guessing patterns from a word file
.TP
.B otpme-dictionary word_export english
Export all words to stdout
.TP
.B otpme-dictionary clear english
Remove all words from the dictionary
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/otpme/
OTPme data directory
